                <pb facs="0550" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve14p2/pg516"/>

                <head>155. Telegram 159191 From the Department of State to the Embassy in the Soviet
                        Union<anchor n="1" xml:id="d155-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1975-07-07T19:13:00+00:00">July 7, 1975, 1913Z</date>.</dateline>
                <p>159191. Subject: Soviet Response on Our Venting Démarche. Ref: State 133038. For USDel—TTB/PNE Talks.</p>
                <p>1. Soviet Embassy today delivered “non-paper” to EUR/SOV desk officer in reply to oral démarche Deputy Assistant
                    Secretary Armitage made June 6 to
                        Vorontsov on venting issue.</p>
                <p>2. Unofficial translation of non-paper as follows: <hi rendition="#italic">Begin
                        text:</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The information on the question raised by the American side is already
                    transmitted to the U.S. Government on March 12,
                    1975. This information contains the answer to the question which was put by the
                    American side and the Soviet side has nothing to add to it.</p>
                <p>At the same time the Soviet side underlines, that the Soviet Union attaches great
                    importance to the compliance with the provisions of the Treaty of Moscow of
                    August 5, 1963 and that appropriate Soviet authorities were and are taking
                    measures directed at strict observance of the requirements of the said treaty.
                        <hi rendition="#italic">End text.</hi>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_KHA_1">
                        Kissinger
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d155-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d155-f1-content">
                <p><seg type="summary">Summary: The Department transmitted the “non-paper” that the
                        Soviet Embassy had delivered in reply to the démarche Deputy Assistant
                        Secretary of State for European Affairs Armitage had made to Soviet Minister Counselor Vorontosov in
                        June and provided an unofficial translation of the paper.</seg></p>
                <p><seg type="source">Source: National Archives, RG
                        59, Central Foreign Policy File, D750234–1086. Secret; Priority. Drafted by
                        Zook; cleared by McNeill, Borg,
                        Ifft, Shinn, and Palmer; approved by Armitage. Repeated for information to the Mission to the
                            IAEA at Vienna and to London. Telegram
                        133038 is <ref target="#d148">Document 148</ref>.</seg></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
